h(2, id: "footnotes") { Footnotes }

p { A definition is a top-level block. A reference is an inline. }

codeblock(lang: "text") {!
p { See the rule.fn(required-title) }

footnote(id: "required-title") { Title is required when meta is present. }
!}

p { The definition needs a non-empty code{id} attribute. The body is prose. }

p { The reference is code{fn(id)} or code{fn("id")}. The identifier form allows letters, digits, underscore, and hyphen. }

p { Checks: }

list {
  item { Duplicate definition ids are a semantic error. }
  item { A reference whose id has no definition is a semantic error. }
  item { Definitions with no references still appear in the footnotes section. }
}

p { Numbering follows first-reference order in the document after includes are merged. Output ids are code{fn-<id>} and code{fnref-<id>}. }

p { This page uses three definitions. The first two are referenced from earlier sections.fn(include-meta) }
